=== Hosts and judges ===
The hosts and judges for the season were announced on ''Good Morning America'' on September 1, 2026, one day before the cast reveal.<ref>{{Cite press release |title=Programming Highlights for ABC News' ''Good Morning America'' and ''GMA3,'' Aug. 31 – Sept. 5 |date=August 28, 2026 |publisher=[[American Broadcasting Company|ABC]] |url=https://www.detpress.com/abcnews/pressrelease/programming-highlights-for-abc-news-good-morning-america-and-gma3-aug-31-sept-5/ |via=[[Disney General Entertainment Content Press]] |access-date=August 29, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260829135941/https://www.detpress.com/abcnews/pressrelease/programming-highlights-for-abc-news-good-morning-america-and-gma3-aug-31-sept-5/ |archive-date=August 29, 2026}}</ref> [[Alfonso Ribeiro]] and [[Julianne Hough]] returned as hosts,<ref name="S35HostsJudges">{{Cite web |last=Nardino |first=Meredith |date=September 1, 2026 |title=''Dancing With the Stars'' Season 35 Judges and Hosts Revealed Before Premiere: Who’s Returning? |url=https://www.usmagazine.com/entertainment/news/dancing-with-the-stars-season-35-judges-and-hosts-revealed/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/archive/SGT7w |archive-date=September 1, 2026 |access-date=September 1, 2026 |website=[[Us Weekly]] |language=en-US}}</ref> while [[Derek Hough]], [[Carrie Ann Inaba]], and [[Bruno Tonioli]] returned as judges.<ref name="S35HostsJudges" /> [[Joe Buck]] served as the guest judge for Super Bowl Night.<ref name="Week5Judge">{{cite web|url=https://abcnews.com/GMA/Culture/joe-buck-guest-judge-dancing-stars-super-bowl/story?id=137080886|title=Joe Buck to guest judge ''Dancing with the Stars'' for 'Super Bowl Night'|work=[[Good Morning America]]|author=Bernabe|date=October 8, 2026|access-date=October 8, 2026|first=Angeline Jane|publisher=[[ABC News (United States)|ABC News]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261008130741/https://abcnews.com/GMA/Culture/joe-buck-guest-judge-dancing-stars-super-bowl/story?id=137080886|archive-date=October 8, 2026|url-status=live}}</ref> [[Kym Johnson]] served as the guest judge for Dedication Night.<ref name="Week6THR">{{Cite web |last=Franklin |first=McKinley |date=October 20, 2026 |title=Grab the Tissues, It’s Dedication Night on ''Dancing With the Stars'': See the Scores, Who Went Home |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-news/dwts-season-35-dedication-week-6-recap-scores-elimination-1236736527/ |access-date=October 21, 2026 |website=[[The Hollywood Reporter]] |language=en-US|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261021191143/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-news/dwts-season-35-dedication-week-6-recap-scores-elimination-1236736527/|archive-date=October 21, 2026|url-status=live}}</ref> [[Shirley Ballas]] served as the guest judge for Horror Movie Night.<ref name="Week7Judge">{{Cite web |last=Murray |first=Tom |date=October 21, 2026 |title=''Strictly'' judge to waltz onto US counterpart ''Dancing with the Stars'' |url=https://www.the-independent.com/arts-entertainment/tv/news/shirley-ballas-strictly-dancing-with-stars-b3070710.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261021190139/https://www.the-independent.com/arts-entertainment/tv/news/shirley-ballas-strictly-dancing-with-stars-b3070710.html |archive-date=October 21, 2026 |access-date=October 21, 2026 |website=[[The Independent]] |language=en}}</ref> [[Cynthia Erivo]] served as the guest judge for Disney Night.<ref name="Week8Judge">{{Cite web |last=Franklin |first=McKinley |date=October 27, 2026 |title=''Dancing With the Stars'' Gets Spooky for Horror Movie Night With the First Perfect Score and a Double Celeb Exit: See the Scores, Who Went Home |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-news/dwts-season-35-horror-movie-week-7-recap-scores-elimination-1236741201/ |access-date=October 28, 2026 |website=[[The Hollywood Reporter]] |language=en-US}}</ref>

The second season of the ''Dancing with the Stars'' podcast, hosted by season thirty-four quarter-finalist [[Andy Richter]], launched on September 10.<ref name="S35PodcastParty">{{Cite press release |title=''Dancing with the Stars'' is Back in the Ballroom with an All-New Cast |date=September 1, 2026 |publisher=[[American Broadcasting Company|ABC]] |url=https://www.detpress.com/abc/pressrelease/dancing-with-the-stars-is-back-in-the-ballroom-with-an-all-new-celebrity-cast-1/ |via=[[Disney General Entertainment Content Press]] |access-date=September 2, 2026|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260902132619/https://www.detpress.com/abc/pressrelease/dancing-with-the-stars-is-back-in-the-ballroom-with-an-all-new-celebrity-cast-1/|archive-date=September 2, 2026}}</ref> An official ''Dancing with the Stars'' [[aftershow]], hosted by season thirty-four champion [[Robert Irwin]], aired live immediately after the second night premiere episode on September 16.<ref name="S35PodcastParty" />

Ritcher revealed the majority of the season's themes during the second episode of the ''Dancing with the Stars'' podcast.<ref name="S35Themes">{{Cite news |last=Cohn |first=Paulette |date=September 18, 2026 |title=''Dancing with the Stars'' Themes for Season 35 Revealed |url=https://parade.com/tv/dancing-with-the-stars-season-35-themes-revealed |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260918195908/https://parade.com/tv/dancing-with-the-stars-season-35-themes-revealed |archive-date=September 18, 2026 |access-date=September 18, 2026 |work=[[Parade (magazine)|Parade]]}}</ref> He did not not reveal the theme for the fifth week of competition;<ref name="S35Themes" /> Super Bowl Night was announced on ''Good Morning America'' on September 30.<ref name="Week5THR">{{Cite web |last=Franklin |first=McKinley |date=September 30, 2026 |title=''Dancing With the Stars'' Sets Super Bowl Night for Oct. 13 |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-news/dancing-with-the-stars-super-bowl-night-october-13-1236716710/ |access-date=September 30, 2026 |website=[[The Hollywood Reporter]] |language=en-US|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260930141734/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-news/dancing-with-the-stars-super-bowl-night-october-13-1236716710/|archive-date=September 30, 2026|url-status=live}}</ref> Throughout the season, Richter shared the songs and dance styles for the upcoming week.<ref name="S&D">Season 35 song and dance styles:
