=== Week 1: Premiere ===
For the two-night season premiere, each couple performed one unlearned dance to a song that topped one of ''[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]'' magazine's [[Billboard charts|music charts]] during the year each celebrity was born.<ref name="Week1PR">{{Cite press release |title=The Ballroom is Back! ''Dancing with the Stars'' Celebrates Season 35 with a Special Two-Night Premiere on ABC and Disney+ |date=September 10, 2026 |publisher=[[American Broadcasting Company|ABC]] |url=https://www.detpress.com/abc/pressrelease/the-ballroom-is-back-dancing-with-the-stars-celebrates-season-35-with-a-special-two-night-premiere-on-abc-and-disney/ |via=[[Disney General Entertainment Content Press]] |access-date=September 10, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260910183627/https://www.detpress.com/abc/pressrelease/the-ballroom-is-back-dancing-with-the-stars-celebrates-season-35-with-a-special-two-night-premiere-on-abc-and-disney/ |archive-date=September 10, 2026}}</ref> The male celebrities performed on the first night and the female celebrities performed on the second night.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Stivale |first=Shelby |date=September 10, 2026 |title=''Dancing With the Stars'' season 35 premiere to end with elimination twist for the first time since 2018 |url=https://ew.com/dancing-with-the-stars-reveals-season-35-premiere-week-elimination-twist-12114436 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260910184852/https://ew.com/dancing-with-the-stars-reveals-season-35-premiere-week-elimination-twist-12114436 |archive-date=September 10, 2026 |access-date=September 10, 2026 |work=[[Entertainment Weekly]]}}</ref> One couple was eliminated at the end of each night.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Siwak |first=Miranda |date=September 10, 2026 |title=''Dancing With the Stars'' Season 35 Will Feature Eliminations on Each Night of Premiere |url=https://www.usmagazine.com/entertainment/news/dancing-with-the-stars-premiere-will-end-with-2-eliminations/ |access-date=September 10, 2026 |website=[[Us Weekly]] |language=en-US|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260910122338/https://www.usmagazine.com/entertainment/news/dancing-with-the-stars-premiere-will-end-with-2-eliminations/|archive-date=September 10, 2026|url-status=live}}</ref>

;Night 1 (Men)

The opening number, choreographed by [[Jamal Sims]], was set to "[[Dancing on My Own]]" by [[Robyn]].<ref name="Week1MenPeople">{{Cite news |last=Kratofil |first=Colleen |date=September 15, 2026 |title=''Dancing with the Stars'' Full Recap: Find Out Who Got Sent Home on Premiere Night After Voting Glitches Rocked the Ballroom |url=https://people.com/dancing-with-the-stars-live-updates-season-35-premiere-night-1-12123487 |access-date=September 15, 2026 |work=[[People (magazine)|People]]|archive-url=https://megalodon.jp/2026-0919-0523-13/https://people.com:443/dancing-with-the-stars-live-updates-season-35-premiere-night-1-12123487|archive-date=September 19, 2026|url-status=live}}</ref> The troupe performed a [[Bumper (broadcasting)|bumper]] to "[[Bangaranga]]" by [[Dara (Bulgarian singer)|Dara]].<ref name="Week1MenPeople" /> Due to technical difficulties, online voting for the night was excluded and only votes cast via [[text messaging]] were accepted.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Longeretta |first=Emily |date=September 15, 2026 |title=''Dancing With the Stars'' Season 35 Kicks Off With Voting Glitch During Premiere |url=https://variety.com/2026/tv/news/dancing-with-the-stars-voting-glitch-season-35-premiere-1236863608/ |access-date=September 15, 2026 |website=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]] |language=en-US|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260916092239/https://variety.com/2026/tv/news/dancing-with-the-stars-voting-glitch-season-35-premiere-1236863608/|archive-date=September 16, 2026|url-status=live}}</ref> The female celebrities and their professional partners performed a routine to "[[The Romantic (album)|Cha Cha Cha]]" by [[Bruno Mars]], choreographed by [[Brandon Armstrong (dancer)|Brandon Armstrong]] and [[Jan Ravnik]].<ref name="Week1MenPeople" /> [[Adele Zaikman]], Allen Genkin, Erik Linder, and Selena Hamilton from ''[[Dancing with the Stars: The Next Pro]]'' performed a [[Salsa (dance)|salsa]] bumper to "[[Dai Dai]]" by [[Shakira]] and [[Burna Boy]].<ref name="Week1MenPeople" /> Inspired by [[Paris Baguette]], one of the season's sponsors, co-host [[Julianne Hough]] and Tessandra Chavez choreographed a number to "[[I Love Paris]]" by [[Tatiana Eva-Marie]] and the Avalon Band; Hough additionally performed the routine with the pros.<ref name="Week1MenPeople" />

