;Night 2 (Women)

The opening number, choreographed by [[Mandy Moore (choreographer)|Mandy Moore]], was set to "[[Love Sensation (Madonna song)|Love Sensation]]" by [[Madonna]].<ref name="Week1WomenPeople">{{Cite news |last=Kratofil |first=Colleen |date=September 16, 2026 |title=''Dancing with the Stars'' Full Recap: 1 Surprising Star Beats Frontrunner Jenna Dewan’s Score While Another Makes Carrie Ann Cry |url=https://people.com/dancing-with-the-stars-live-updates-ladies-hit-the-ballroom-premiere-night-2-12124892 |access-date=September 16, 2026 |work=[[People (magazine)|People]]|archive-url=https://megalodon.jp/2026-0919-0528-49/https://people.com:443/dancing-with-the-stars-live-updates-ladies-hit-the-ballroom-premiere-night-2-12124892|archive-date=September 19, 2026|url-status=live}}</ref> The troupe performed a number to "[[Danceteria (song)|Danceteria]]" by Madonna and a [[tango]] bumper to "[[Pinky Up]]" by [[Katseye]].<ref name="Week1WomenPeople" /> Singer-songwriter [[BC Jean]] performed "[[Black Velvet (song)|Black Velvet]]" by [[Alannah Myles]] for [[Maura Higgins]]' [[foxtrot]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=DeGrazia |first=Leah |date=September 16, 2026 |title=''DWTS''{{'}} Mark Ballas Reveals How Wife BC Jean Saved Maura Higgins Routine Last-Minute |url=https://www.eonline.com/news/1436171/mark-ballas-wife-bc-jean-sings-song-for-dwts-performance |access-date=September 16, 2026 |website=[[E! News]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260917061920/https://www.eonline.com/news/1436171/mark-ballas-wife-bc-jean-sings-song-for-dwts-performance|archive-date=September 17, 2026|url-status=live}}</ref> Inspired by [[Google Gemini]], one of the season's sponsors, judge [[Derek Hough]] and Tessandra Chavez choreographed a number to "Asturias Variations" by [[Isaac Albéniz]] and "[[11:11 (Rodrigo y Gabriela album)|Hanuman]]" by [[Rodrigo y Gabriela]].<ref name="Week1WomenPeople" /> Hough additionally performed the routine with his wife [[Hayley Erbert]] and dancers who were featured in their Symphony of Dance stage tour.<ref name="Week1WomenPeople" />

