=== Week 5: Super Bowl Night ===
''Individual judges' scores in the charts below (given in parentheses) are listed in this order from left to right: Carrie Ann Inaba, Derek Hough, [[Joe Buck]], Bruno Tonioli.''

To commemorate [[Super Bowl LXI]], each couple performed one unlearned dance to songs that were performed in various [[List of Super Bowl halftime shows|Super Bowl halftime shows]].<ref name="Week5THR" /> ''[[Monday Night Football]]'' play-by-play commentator [[Joe Buck]] appeared as a guest judge.<ref name="Week5Judge" /> The opening number, choreographed by [[Jamal Sims]], was set to "[[Nuevayol]]" by [[Bad Bunny]], "[[Rude Boy (Rihanna song)|Rude Boy]]" by [[Rihanna]], and "[[Humble (song)|Humble]]" by [[Kendrick Lamar]].<ref name="Week5PR" /> It featured appearances from [[Dancing with the Stars (American TV series) season 3|season three]] champion [[Emmitt Smith]] and [[Dancing with the Stars (American TV series) season 14|season fourteen]] champion [[Donald Driver]].<ref name="Week5PR" />

[[Britt Stewart]] and [[Brandon Armstrong (dancer)|Brandon Armstrong]] performed a bumper to "[[Bootylicious]]" by [[Destiny's Child]].<ref name="Week5PR" /> Smith and Driver joined [[Dancing with the Stars (American TV series) season 27|season twenty-seven]] contestant [[DeMarcus Ware]] and [[Dancing with the Stars (American TV series) season 33|season thirty-three]] finalist [[Danny Amendola]] in a number to "[[Heavy Action|It's Heavy Action (''Monday Night Football'' Theme)]]" by [[APM Music|APM]] and "[[In the Air Tonight]]" by [[Chris Stapleton]].<ref name="Week5PR">{{Cite press release |title=''Dancing with the Stars'' Brings the Biggest Hits to the Ballroom with 'Super Bowl Night' on ABC and Disney+ |date=October 8, 2026 |publisher=[[American Broadcasting Company|ABC]] |url=https://www.detpress.com/abc/pressrelease/dancing-with-the-stars-brings-the-biggest-hits-to-the-ballroom-with-super-bowl-night-on-abc-and-disney/ |access-date=October 8, 2026|via=[[Disney General Entertainment Content Press]]|archive-url=https://megalodon.jp/2026-1009-0218-40/https://www.detpress.com:443/abc/pressrelease/dancing-with-the-stars-brings-the-biggest-hits-to-the-ballroom-with-super-bowl-night-on-abc-and-disney/|archive-date=October 9, 2026}}</ref> It was choreographed by Sims and the [[List of Super Bowl champions|Super Bowl champions]] performed with [[Hailey Bills]], Onye Stevenson, [[Britt Stewart]], and [[Adele Zaikman]].<ref name="Week5PR" /> [[Julia Stiles]]' [[Jazz dance|jazz]] routine featured a cameo appearance from her ''[[Save the Last Dance]]'' (2001) co-star [[Sean Patrick Thomas]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Chaudhry |first=Sameen |date=October 14, 2026 |title=''DWTS'' – Julia Stiles taps ''Save the Last Dance'' star Sean Patrick Thomas |url=https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/tv-streaming/2026/10/14/julia-stiles-dwts-sean-patrick-thomas-save-the-last-dance/92245738007/ |access-date=October 14, 2026 |website=[[USA Today]] |language=en-US|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261014191636/https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/tv-streaming/2026/10/14/julia-stiles-dwts-sean-patrick-thomas-save-the-last-dance/92245738007/|archive-date=October 14, 2026|url-status=live}}</ref>

