=== Week 6: Dedication Night ===
''Individual judges' scores in the charts below (given in parentheses) are listed in this order from left to right: Carrie Ann Inaba, Derek Hough, [[Kym Johnson]], Bruno Tonioli.''

Each couple performed one unlearned dance to honor the most influential figures and institutions in the celebrities' lives.<ref name="Week6PR">{{Cite press release |title=''Dancing with the Stars'' Brings Heart and Meaning to the Ballroom with 'Dedication Night' on ABC and Disney+ |date=October 15, 2026 |publisher=[[American Broadcasting Company|ABC]] |url=https://www.detpress.com/abc/pressrelease/dancing-with-the-stars-brings-heart-and-meaning-to-the-ballroom-with-dedication-night-on-abc-and-disney/ |via=[[Disney General Entertainment Content Press]] |access-date=October 15, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261015130557/https://www.detpress.com/abc/pressrelease/dancing-with-the-stars-brings-heart-and-meaning-to-the-ballroom-with-dedication-night-on-abc-and-disney/ |archive-date=October 15, 2026}}</ref> There was no elimination this week; all scores were carried over to the following week.<ref name="Week6THR" /> Two-time mirrorball champion [[Kym Johnson]] returned as a guest judge for the second consecutive year.<ref name="Week6PR" /> [[Valentin Chmerkovskiy|Val Chmerkovskiy]] was suspended from participating in this episode after he made inappropriate remarks on social media against judge [[Carrie Ann Inaba]] that referenced [[Chris Rock–Will Smith slapping incident|actor Will Smith slapping comedian Chris Rock during the 94th Academy Awards]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Evans |first=Greg |date=October 17, 2026 |title=''Dancing With The Stars'' Suspends Val Chmerkovskiy For TikTok Referencing Will Smith Oscar Moment; Dancer Responds, “Instinct Was To Defend My Wife” |url=https://deadline.com/2026/10/val-chmerkovskiy-dancing-with-the-stars-suspension-1237166428/ |access-date=October 17, 2026 |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]] |language=en-US|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261017211302/https://deadline.com/2026/10/val-chmerkovskiy-dancing-with-the-stars-suspension-1237166428/|archive-date=October 17, 2026|url-status=live}}</ref> It marked the first time a professional dancer had been suspended in ''Dancing with the Stars'' history.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Speakman |first=Kimberlee |date=October 17, 2026 |title=Val Chmerkovskiy Pulled from ''DWTS'' After Oscars Slap Comment, the First Pro Suspension in the Series’ History |url=https://people.com/val-chmerkovskiy-pulled-from-dwts-after-oscars-slap-comment-12179630 |access-date=October 17, 2026 |work=[[People (magazine)|People]]|archive-url=https://megalodon.jp/2026-1018-0700-55/https://people.com:443/val-chmerkovskiy-pulled-from-dwts-after-oscars-slap-comment-12179630|archive-date=October 18, 2026|url-status=live}}</ref> As a result, [[Jenna Dewan]] performed her [[Viennese waltz]] with [[Alan Bersten]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Longeretta |first=Emily |date=October 17, 2026 |title=''Dancing With the Stars'' Pulls Val Chmerkovskiy After ‘Inappropriate’ Carrie Ann Inaba Slap Joke: ‘The Well-Being’ of Our Staff Is ‘Non-Negotiable’ |url=https://variety.com/2026/tv/news/dancing-with-the-stars-pulls-val-chmerkovskiy-carrie-ann-inaba-slap-joke-1236915031/ |access-date=October 17, 2026 |website=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]] |language=en-US|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261017211719/https://variety.com/2026/tv/news/dancing-with-the-stars-pulls-val-chmerkovskiy-carrie-ann-inaba-slap-joke-1236915031/|archive-date=October 17, 2026|url-status=live}}</ref> 

For the second consecutive year, the friends, family members, and special guests selected by each celebrity contestant were incorporated into their routines.<ref name="Week6PR" /> For her Viennese waltz, [[Tatyana Ali]] was joined by her ''[[The Fresh Prince of Bel-Air]]'' (1990–1996) co-star [[Alfonso Ribeiro]].<ref name="Week6Parade">{{Cite news |last=Galante |first=Grace |date=October 18, 2026 |title=Alfonso Ribeiro to Join 1 ''DWTS'' Couple's Performance on 'Dedication Night' |url=https://parade.com/news/alfonso-ribeiro-join-tatyana-ali-jan-ravnik-performance-dwts-dedication-night |access-date=October 18, 2026 |work=[[Parade (magazine)|Parade]] |language=en|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261020144746/https://parade.com/news/alfonso-ribeiro-join-tatyana-ali-jan-ravnik-performance-dwts-dedication-night|archive-date=October 20, 2026|url-status=live}}</ref> She also performed "[[(You Don't Know) How Glad I Am]]" by [[Nancy Wilson (jazz singer)|Nancy Wilson]].<ref name="Week6Parade" /> [[Maura Higgins]] was joined by professional [[Irish stepdance|Irish stepdancer]] Lochlan "Lucky" Howard for her [[Pasodoble|paso doble]].<ref name="Week6People">{{Cite news |last=Kratofil |first=Colleen |date=October 20, 2026 |title=''Dancing with the Stars'' Recap: Dedication Night Brought Tears, a Pregnancy Announcement and an Elimination Shock |url=https://people.com/dancing-with-the-stars-live-blog-dedication-night-12184773 |access-date=October 20, 2026 |work=[[People (magazine)|People]]}}</ref> [[Tyler Cameron]] was joined by his fiancée Tate Madden for his [[Contemporary dance|contemporary]] routine.<ref name="Week6People" /> During the performance, the couple revealed that Madden was pregnant with their first child, a daughter.<ref name="Week6People" /> At the end of her contemporary routine, [[Julia Stiles]] was joined by her ''[[10 Things I Hate About You]]'' (1999) co-stars [[Joseph Gordon-Levitt]], [[Larisa Oleynik]], [[Andrew Keegan]], [[Gabrielle Union]], and [[Susan May Pratt]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Frank |first=Jason P. |date=October 21, 2026 |title=Julia Stiles Danced for Heath Ledger on ''Dancing With the Stars'' |url=https://www.vulture.com/article/julia-stiles-heath-ledger-tribute-dancing-with-the-stars.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261021184338/https://www.vulture.com/article/julia-stiles-heath-ledger-tribute-dancing-with-the-stars.html |archive-date=October 21, 2026 |access-date=October 21, 2026 |website=[[Vulture (website)|Vulture]] |language=en}}</ref>

The troupe performed a bumper to "[[Stay (If You Wanna Dance)]]" by [[Myles Smith]].<ref name="Week6PR" /> [[Hailey Bills]] and [[Brandon Armstrong (dancer)|Brandon Armstrong]] performed a bumper to "[[Fever Dream (song)|Fever Dream]]" by [[Alex Warren]].<ref name="Week6PR" /> [[Adele Zaikman]] and Allen Genkin honored [[Dolly Parton]] with a performance to "[[Here You Come Again (song)|Here You Come Again]]" by Parton and [[Willa Amai]].<ref name="Week6PR" /> Genkin, the eliminated pros, and the troupe performed a number to "[[The Cat in the Hat (2026 film)#Music|CATastrophe]]" by [[Hilary Duff]] from ''[[The Cat in the Hat (2026 film)|The Cat in the Hat]]'' (2026).<ref name="Week6PR" /> It was choreographed by Bills and Bersten and featured an appearance from [[Dancing with the Stars (American TV series) season 32|season thirty-two]] champion [[Xochitl Gomez]].<ref name="Week6People" />

