=== Week 7: Horror Movie Night ===
''Individual judges' scores in the charts below (given in parentheses) are listed in this order from left to right: Carrie Ann Inaba, Derek Hough, [[Shirley Ballas]], Bruno Tonioli.''

Each couple performed one unlearned dance inspired by [[Horror film|horror films]].<ref name="Week7PR">{{Cite press release |title=''Dancing with the Stars'' Serves Up Spooks and Scares with 'Horror Movie Night' |date=October 22, 2026 |publisher=[[American Broadcasting Company|ABC]] |url=https://www.detpress.com/abc/pressrelease/dancing-with-the-stars-serves-up-spooks-and-scares-with-horror-movie-night/ |via=[[Disney General Entertainment Content Press]] |access-date=October 22, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261023003142/https://www.detpress.com/abc/pressrelease/dancing-with-the-stars-serves-up-spooks-and-scares-with-horror-movie-night/ |archive-date=October 23, 2026}}</ref> There was a double elimination this week.<ref name="Week7PR" /> ''[[Strictly Come Dancing]]'' and ''[[Dancing with the Stars: The Next Pro]]'' head judge [[Shirley Ballas]] appeared as a guest judge.<ref name="Week7Judge" /> [[Valentin Chmerkovskiy|Val Chmerkovskiy]] returned to compete with [[Jenna Dewan]] after he was suspended last week.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Franklin |first=McKinley |date=October 21, 2026 |title=Val Chmerkovskiy Returns to ''Dancing With the Stars'' After One-Episode Suspension |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-news/val-back-dancing-with-stars-season-35-suspension-jenna-dewan-1236736004/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261022145117/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-news/val-back-dancing-with-stars-season-35-suspension-jenna-dewan-1236736004/ |archive-date=October 22, 2026 |access-date=October 22, 2026 |website=[[The Hollywood Reporter]] |language=en-US}}</ref> The opening number, performed by the eliminated pros and the troupe, was set to "[[Tubular Bells]]" by [[Mike Oldfield]].<ref name="Week7PR" /> The troupe performed bumpers to "[[Beetlejuice Beetlejuice (soundtrack)|Main Title Theme (from ''Beetlejuice Beetlejuice'')]]" by [[Danny Elfman]] and "[[Magic (The Cars song)|Magic]]" by [[Hailee Steinfeld]]; the latter was choreographed by [[Brandon Armstrong (dancer)|Brandon Armstrong]].<ref name="Week7PR" /> Singer-songwriter [[BC Jean]] performed "Madness" by [[Ruelle (singer)|Ruelle]] for [[Ezra Frech]]'s [[Jazz dance|jazz]] routine and "[[Cry Little Sister]]" by [[Gerard McMahon]] for [[Maura Higgins]]' [[Contemporary dance|contemporary]] routine.<ref name="Week7PR" /> [[Britt Stewart]] and [[Alan Bersten]] performed a bumper to "[[Wuthering Heights (soundtrack)|Dying for You]]" by [[Charli XCX]].<ref name="Week7PR" />

