=== Week 8: Disney Night ===
''Individual judges' scores in the charts below (given in parentheses) are listed in this order from left to right: Carrie Ann Inaba, Derek Hough, [[Cynthia Erivo]], Bruno Tonioli.''

To avoid conflicts with the [[2026 United States elections|U.S. midterm elections]], held on November 3, 2026, ''Dancing with the Stars'' moved the air date of this episode to Monday, one day earlier.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Bonner |first=Mehera |date=October 28, 2026 |title=Here’s Why ''Dancing With the Stars'' Is on Monday Night Next Week |url=https://www.cosmopolitan.com/entertainment/tv/a74269776/why-is-dancing-with-the-stars-on-monday-next-week/ |access-date=October 28, 2026 |website=[[Cosmopolitan (magazine)|Cosmopolitan]] |language=en-US|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261028140857/https://www.cosmopolitan.com/entertainment/tv/a74269776/why-is-dancing-with-the-stars-on-monday-next-week/|archive-date=October 28, 2026|url-status=live}}</ref> Each couple performed one unlearned dance and participated in a team dance to songs from the ''[[Disney Theatrical Productions|Disney on Broadway]]'' series of [[Musical theatre|musicals]] and [[Play (theatre)|stage plays]].<ref name="Week8PR">{{Cite press release |title=''Dancing with the Stars'' Sets the Stage for a Magical 'Disney Night' on ABC and Disney+ |date=October 29, 2026 |publisher=[[American Broadcasting Company|ABC]] |url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261030000244/https://www.detpress.com/abc/pressrelease/dancing-with-the-stars-sets-the-stage-for-a-magical-disney-night-on-abc-and-disney/ |via=[[Disney General Entertainment Content Press]] |access-date=October 29, 2026 |archive-url=https://www.detpress.com/abc/pressrelease/dancing-with-the-stars-sets-the-stage-for-a-magical-disney-night-on-abc-and-disney/ |archive-date=October 30, 2026}}</ref> Actress and singer [[Cynthia Erivo]] appeared as a guest judge.<ref name="Week8Judge" /> The teams were chosen by the celebrities with the lowest combined scores, [[Tatyana Ali]] and [[Connor Wood (comedian)|Connor Wood]].<ref name="Week8PR" /> For the second consecutive year, co-hosts [[Alfonso Ribeiro]] and [[Julianne Hough]] each joined a team.<ref name="Week8PR" />

The opening number, choreographed by Joey Pizzi, was set to a medley of four musicals and featured appearances from several vocalists: "[[Circle of Life|Circle of Life/Nants Ingonyama]]" from ''[[The Lion King (musical)|The Lion King]]'' featuring [[Heather Headley]], Selloane Nkhela, and the musical's cast; "Belle" from ''[[Beauty and the Beast (musical)|Beauty and the Beast]]'' featuring Kyra Belle Johnson; "Seize the Day" from ''[[Newsies (musical)|Newsies]]''; and "[[The Greatest Show]]" from ''[[The Greatest Showman (musical)|The Greatest Showman]]''.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Quinn |first=Dave |date=October 29, 2026 |title=''DWTS'' Will Celebrate Decades of Disney on Broadway with Performances by Sherri Shepherd, Heather Headley and More (Exclusive) |url=https://people.com/dancing-with-the-stars-disney-on-broadway-night-exclusive-details-12197818 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://megalodon.jp/2026-1102-1121-36/https://people.com:443/dancing-with-the-stars-disney-on-broadway-night-exclusive-details-12197818 |archive-date=November 2, 2026 |access-date=November 1, 2026 |work=[[People (magazine)|People]]}}</ref> Additionally, Headley performed "[[Elton John and Tim Rice's Aida|Easy as Life]]" for Ali's [[Contemporary dance|contemporary]] routine and "[[I See the Light]]" for Wood's [[waltz]]; Johnson performed "[[Supercalifragilisticexpialidocious]]" for [[Harry Shum Jr.]]'s [[Jazz dance|jazz]] routine; [[Michael James Scott]] performed "[[Under the Sea]]" for [[Ezra Frech]]'s [[Samba (ballroom dance)|samba]]; and Rodney Ingram performed "[[Be Our Guest]]" for [[Jenna Dewan]]'s [[quickstep]].<ref name="Week8PR" /> [[Dancing with the Stars (American TV series) season 14|Season fourteen]] contestant [[Sherri Shepherd]] and Ingram joined [[Britt Stewart]], [[Brandon Armstrong (dancer)|Brandon Armstrong]], the troupe for a performance to "[[Friend Like Me]]" from ''[[Aladdin (2011 musical)|Aladdin]]'', choreographed by Stewart.<ref name="Week8PR" /><ref>{{cite web|url= https://www.broadwayworld.com/article/Heather-Headley-Sherri-Shepherd-More-to-Perform-on-DANCING-WITH-THE-STARS-Disney-Night-20261030?fbclid=PAVERFWAVRq7lleHRuA2FlbQIxMABwZG9mAmZkaWQWURSjEHdf1BMzS8zbsSJ_OceE15jF0nNydGMGYXBwX2lkDzEyNDAyNDU3NDI4NzQxNAABp3-tigB9Tw6q5DHhTNQd9Hw2aTuLCjPRea2iFnA1YtsIGZ_w6AMkYj1bTPOl_aem_RiZu-DY_cWGNTdwsvFsbGA|title=Heather Headley, Sherri Shepherd & More to Perform on ''Dancing with the Stars'' Disney Night|publisher=Broadway World|accessdate= October 30, 2026|date=October 30, 2026|website=[[BroadwayWorld]]|last=Major|first=Michael|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261102023023/https://www.broadwayworld.com/article/Heather-Headley-Sherri-Shepherd-More-to-Perform-on-DANCING-WITH-THE-STARS-Disney-Night-20261030|archive-date=November 2, 2026|url-status=live}}</ref>

