=== Week 9: Grammy Night ===
To commemorate the [[69th Annual Grammy Awards]], each couple will perform one unlearned dance to songs that either won or were nominated for a [[Grammy Awards|Grammy Award]].<ref name="Week9PR">{{Cite press release |title=''Dancing with the Stars'' Brings the Biggest Names and Hits in Music to the Ballroom with 'Grammy Night' on ABC and Disney+ |date=November 4, 2026 |publisher=[[American Broadcasting Company|ABC]] |url=https://www.detpress.com/abc/pressrelease/dancing-with-the-stars-brings-the-biggest-names-and-hits-in-music-to-the-ballroom-with-grammy-night-on-abc-and-disney/ |via=[[Disney General Entertainment Content Press]] |access-date=November 4, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261104220439/https://www.detpress.com/abc/pressrelease/dancing-with-the-stars-brings-the-biggest-names-and-hits-in-music-to-the-ballroom-with-grammy-night-on-abc-and-disney/ |archive-date=November 4, 2026}}</ref> Six couples will also participate in a dance-off for extra points, which will feature live performances from [[Dancing with the Stars (American TV series) season 11|season eleven]] semi-finalist [[Brandy Norwood|Brandy]], [[Monica (singer)|Monica]], [[Maren Morris]] and [[Sheryl Crow]].<ref name="Week9PR" /> For earning the highest cumulative points in the season so far, [[Harry Shum Jr.]] & [[Jenna Johnson]] earned immunity from the dance-offs and automatically received bonus points.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Bonner |first=Mehera |date=November 3, 2026 |title=One Celebrity Just Got Immunity on ''Dancing With the Stars'' Next Week |url=https://www.cosmopolitan.com/entertainment/tv/a74321322/who-got-immunity-dancing-with-the-stars/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261103143534/https://www.cosmopolitan.com/entertainment/tv/a74321322/who-got-immunity-dancing-with-the-stars/ |archive-date=November 3, 2026 |access-date=November 3, 2026 |website=[[Cosmopolitan (magazine)|Cosmopolitan]] |language=en-US}}</ref> Additional pro and troupe performances will be set to "[[Just Keep Watching]]" by [[Tate McRae]], "[[Good Luck, Babe!]]" by [[Chappell Roan]], "[[As It Was]]" by [[Harry Styles]], and "[[Radioactive (Imagine Dragons song)|Radioactive]]" by [[Imagine Dragons]].<ref name="Week9PR" /> 

